id: pm-ts-starter-tezw
title: Scope the json renderer to the commands this extension owns so it stops colliding with sibling extensions
description: "The json renderer was registered through the unscoped defineRendererOverride overload, so the host treated it as owning every command. Two consequences: it was the last remaining extension_renderer_collision in the 17-package fleet union (against pm-context, which declares ownership correctly), and an unscoped renderer is one guard-bug away from replacing all pm --json output. The SDK exposes a scoped overload taking ScopedRendererOverrideDefinition {commands?, resultDiscriminator?, run}, and the declarative renderers map accepts it, so ownership can be declared without leaving the blueprint style this package demonstrates. Deliberately excludes list: this extension overrides the list command, but that override returns ctx.result untouched, so list never produces a payload the renderer should reshape."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: collisions,ownership,renderers,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:09:13.600Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T18:23:18.233Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-05T18:23:18.215Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-05T18:23:18.215Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: The json renderer declares a non-empty commands list plus a resultDiscriminator; the renderer declines a command it does not own even when handed this extension's own payload; list is not in the owned set; pm health on the fleet union reports zero extension_renderer_collision warnings; all tests pass and typecheck is clean.
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T18:09:25.281Z","harness:claude-code","VERIFIED IN THE REAL UNION, not just in tests.\n\nMethod: installed the 17 published fleet packages into a clean scratch workspace on pm-cli 2026.8.5, then swapped this package's freshly built dist into the installed extension directory and re-ran pm health.\n\nMeasured progression of total extension warnings in that union:\n- 20 on pm-cli 2026.8.3 (9 of them renderer collisions)\n- 12 on 2026.8.5, after upstream PR 893 taught the collision check to suppress statically disjoint ownership (renderer collisions 9 -> 1; the 1 was this package)\n- 11 with this change: extension_renderer_collision no longer appears at all\n\nConfirmed disjoint from every sibling that declares ownership: pm-starter owns ['starter demo'], pm-context owns ['context-pack','context-handoff','context-usage'], pm-changelog owns ['changelog generate','changelog export'], pm-ops owns OPS_COMMAND_PATHS. This package's owned set is 'hello' plus the ts-starter and ts-starter-demo paths, which intersects none of them.\n\nThe SDK test harness ENFORCES the ownership list, which is how the pre-existing renderer test caught it: that test passed command 'ts-starter-demo', which is not a real command path (the real ones are 'ts-starter-demo import' and 'ts-starter-demo export'), so once ownership was declared the renderer correctly declined and the assertion failed. Corrected the test to a real owned path rather than widening ownership to match the test."
  "2026-08-05T18:18:38.019Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 applied. CodeRabbit (Major, functional correctness) was right that the ownership set over-claimed and that the test checked a prefix rather than an exact set.\n\nNarrowed to exactly one command: 'ts-starter-demo export'. Verified by tracing every payload site - grep for ts_starter finds a single producing return in the whole file, demoExporter's { ts_starter: true, exported: 0 }. demoImporter returns { imported: 0 }, listCommandOverride returns ctx.result untouched, and no command handler emits a ts_starter shape at all. So the earlier 9-command list asserted ownership the extension never exercises.\n\nDid NOT adopt CodeRabbit's literal suggestion of {hello, ts-starter, ts-starter-demo import, ts-starter-demo export}: 'ts-starter' is not a command path (the real paths are 'ts-starter info', 'ts-starter plan-demo', and so on), and neither hello nor the importer produces a renderable payload. The finding was correct, the proposed set was not.\n\nTest now asserts deepStrictEqual against the exact single-element set, so a future widening of the claim fails the suite instead of passing a prefix match.\n\nRe-verified in the union after the change: 11 warnings, ZERO renderer collisions. Coverage still 90.67/70.79/75.00 against the ratcheted 90/70/75. 52/52 tests pass."
close_reason: "Renderer ownership declared and narrowed to the exact producing command. Verified in the installed 17-package union: zero renderer collisions. CI green on both Node versions, 52/52 tests, coverage 90.67/70.79/75.00 against ratcheted 90/70/75, changelog check clean. CodeRabbit's Major finding applied and acknowledged by the bot as resolved; Greptile 5/5 with no findings."
body: ""
